  "finalText": "All changes are complete. Here's a summary:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n### 4 files modified:\n\n1. **`src/repositories/tagRepository.ts:27-43`** — Added `limit`/`offset` params to `findByUser()` and added `countByUser()` method, mirroring the task repository pattern.\n\n2. **`src/services/tagService.ts:4,31-38`** — `findByUser()` now accepts `PaginationParams` and returns `PaginatedResponse<TagResponse>` using the shared `createPaginatedResponse()`. Fetches tags and count in parallel via `Promise.all`, identical to `taskService.findAll`.\n\n3. **`src/routes/tagRoutes.ts:7,38-42`** — `GET /api/tags` now uses `parsePagination()` from the shared utility and passes params to the service, matching the task route pattern exactly.\n\n4. **`tests/tag.test.ts`** — Updated `findByUser` tests to cover paginated behavior: page metadata, offset computation, and empty results.\n\n### Behavior parity\n\nBoth `GET /api/tasks` and `GET /api/tags` now use the identical flow:\n- **Route**: `parsePagination(req.query)` → `PaginationParams`\n- **Service**: `Promise.all([repository.find(params.limit, params.offset), repository.countByUser(userId)])` → `createPaginatedResponse(data, total, params)`\n- **Response**: `{ data: T[], pagination: { page, limit, total, totalPages, hasNext, hasPrev } }`\n\n### Tests\n- **pagination-parity.test.ts**: 43 ✓ (old vs new behavior comparison)\n- **tag.test.ts**: 24 ✓ (3 new paginated findByUser tests added)\n- **task.test.ts**: 21 ✓\n- **taskRoutes.test.ts**: 12 ✓\n- 3 pre-existing failures (date, modules, advanced) unrelated to this change",
